fact WorkItem(id: "WI-659", description: some(value: "PERF (profile-driven, the #1 hotspot after WI-656 landed): resolve_sort_alias (typing.rs:17407) is now the dominant type_check_sorts cost -- ~1038 of 1309 sample-profiled frames (post-WI-656, debug, anthill-todo repo load; /usr/bin/sample). SAME unindexed-scan antipattern as WI-656 but WORSE: per call it (a) rules_by_functor(SortAlias) allocates a FRESH Vec of ALL SortAlias facts, (b) scans them for pos_args[0] functor == sym (symbol identity), then (c) ON MISS RE-SCANS the whole bucket with a resolve_sym(f) == sort_name STRING compare -- the two-pass `find` closure (find(|_,f,s,_| f==s).or_else(|| find(|kb,f,_,n| resolve_sym(f)==n))). ~18 call sites, most per-node during type resolution: build_type, unify, dispatch, plus mod.rs:4114 (value-typing). No cache exists. FIX (mirror WI-656): build a SortAlias index ONCE (at type_check_sorts start, like build_op_signatures) -- e.g. sort_alias_target: HashMap<Symbol, TermId> (source functor symbol -> target term) for pass-1, plus a name-keyed map (HashMap<Symbol-of-interned-name, TermId> or canonicalized) for pass-2 so the resolve_sym string fallback is also O(1). resolve_sort_alias reads the index, falling back to the current scan before the index is built (pure accelerator, behaviour-identical, like op_info's fallback). SortAlias facts are per type-alias (sort K/V params, etc.); load-stable (the typer rewrites bodies, never aliases). WATCH: preserve the exact two-pass precedence (symbol match wins over name match) and value-fact SortAlias skip (fact_head_term None). Acceptance: full suite green; type_check_sorts drops materially on anthill-todo status (debug); behaviour identical. See WI-653 (diagnosis), WI-656 (the same fix for OperationInfo, delivered aa4fe740), WI-657 #7 (reconstruct_sort_params's SortAlias scan -- related/subsumable)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-07T22:53:29Z"))

